        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "It looks like your command is slightly off.\n\nTo run a Python file, the correct format is:\n\n```bash\npython condoliving_generator.py\n```\n\n### If that doesn’t work, try these depending on your system:\n\n**Windows (most common):**\n```bash\npy condoliving_generator.py\n```\n\n**Or explicitly:**\n```bash\npython3 condoliving_generator.py\n```\n\n---\n\n### Common issues to check:\n\n1. **Wrong folder**\nMake sure you're in the same directory as the file:\n```bash\ncd path\\to\\your\\folder\n```\n\n2. **File name typo**\nConfirm the file is exactly:\n```\ncondoliving_generator.py\n```\n\n3. **Python not installed / not added to PATH**\nCheck:\n```bash\npython --version\n```\n\nor\n```bash\npy --version\n```\n\n---\n\nIf you want, paste the exact error message you’re getting and I’ll fix it with you step-by-step."
          ]
        },
